Section 6: Quality Assessment (Risk of Bias / PROBAST)
	•	Participants (Selection Bias): High Risk | Quote/Reasoning: This was a retrospective single-center study of 576 recipients from one institution, which limits representativeness despite a decent sample size.  ￼
	•	Predictors (Input Variable Bias): Low Risk | Quote/Reasoning: Predictors were donor and recipient variables “known at the time of donor offer acceptance,” making them appropriately timed and clinically relevant for prediction.  ￼
	•	Outcome (Definition Bias): Low Risk | Quote/Reasoning: PGD grade 3 was defined according to International Society for Heart and Lung Transplant criteria and graded by two board-certified pulmonologists.  ￼
	•	Analysis (Modeling Bias): Unclear | Quote/Reasoning: Strengths include lasso feature reduction, train/test splitting, 5-fold CV with random grid search, 50 bootstrap iterations, and formal calibration assessment. Uncertainty remains because discrimination was only modest and no external validation was reported.  ￼
	•	Applicability to Review Question: Low Concern | Quote/Reasoning: The study directly addresses AI/ML prediction of PGD after lung transplantation using donor-recipient clinical data and is highly relevant to the review question.  ￼

